  "details": "[The following is a bug report from @Shiduki_Saku that I have translated from Japanese]\n[It’s not entirely clear when this broke, but it was likely working on April 23rd at least. I’ve asked Shiduki for more details if possible.]\n\nWorld ID: wrld_9ab437bf-79c4-4747-8cbf-8d3a09768f05\nWorld ID with workaround in place (synchronize physics off): wrld_1da7dd95-0580-427e-80c2-686971e316ab\n\nReproduction steps:\n\nUser A creates (and joins) an instance of the above world. User B joins the instance. User A sees the world properly, but user B sees some objects in a different position (both static and non-static objects). [1] is a screenshot from user A’s point of view, [2] is a screenshot from user B; parts of the elevator are in a shifted position.\n\nEdit: The bug was worked around by unchecking synchronize physics. Shiduki will be uploading the broken version under a separate ID for bug reproduction purposes.\n\n[1] https://www.dropbox.com/s/scobofjea6eha4v/elevator%20bug%20user%20a.jpg?dl=0\n[2] https://www.dropbox.com/s/g25ovcztj43s8fc/elevator%20bug%20user%20b.jpg?dl=0",
